﻿
    [1]: https://i.stack.imgur.com/HrzZh.png

[1]: https://i.stack.imgur.com/HrzZh.png

I am unable to get more than 16 elements in the ArrayList after a point and also, my code coverage and Pex method generation keep failing after the 16th element. 

A: Arrays in .NET are fixed size: the size is set when you declare the array, and cannot be changed once the array is full. The maximum size of a standard array is Int32.MaxValue, or about 2 billion, which is significantly much lower than the theoretical maximum of a ArrayList which can handle over 20 billion elements.
You can pass larger sets of data without any problem. The only thing you have to pay attention to is the performance.
If you're testing ArrayList but encounter problems with the size, perhaps you're not looking at the right unit tests. Unit tests should cover the functional requirements (methods) without overloading system constraints (arrays).
Here's an example of code coverage over ArrayList.
